  "_about": "Crossroads as a zone plan for the vertical slice (Claude A, 25 Oct; docs/vision/vertical-slice.md). Shaped like art/regions/*.json (id, box, tiers with outlines, routes, stairs, places) plus what a playable zone needs: buildings, lots, props, people, spawns, doors, restores, stages and raid pads. World px, local to the zone, origin at the top-left; origin_on_canvas maps it onto the 11264 x 6912 world canvas (the square sits where art/regions/valley.json puts it: 6176, 3448). 'if' is a quest condition (core/quests.gd): an item shows only while it holds, so one plan holds the broken and the restored town. game/tools/gen_blockout.py writes zones/crossroads/crossroads.tscn from it; core/village.gd reads restores and stages. Every rectangle is a blockout placeholder, not art.",
